 "stdout": "The new card works for direct card-based creation, but legacy Gemini configurations retain the model that the change identifies as unavailable. The advertised setup documentation is also missing.\n\nFull review comments:\n\n- [P2] Update the legacy Gemini default model too — C:\\Users\\user\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\07f6cb4a104ab615\\b45469f7-16ea-4066-9a93-2d3ba89b7e77\\scratchpad\\r1\\work\\T2-incumbent\\app\\provider_catalog.py:43-44\n  Users configured through the legacy `.env`/settings path still get `gemini-2.5-flash`: `app/config.py`, `.env.example`, and `docker-compose.yml` retain that default, and migration copies `settings.GEMINI_MODEL` into the saved Gemini connection. Thus a new deployment with `GEMINI_API_KEYS` (or an existing legacy configuration) continues to hit the model this change says is unavailable to new users, rather than the new card default.\n\n- [P2] Add the referenced Vertex setup guide — C:\\Users\\user\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\07f6cb4a104ab615\\b45469f7-16ea-4066-9a93-2d3ba89b7e77\\scratchpad\\r1\\work\\T2-incumbent\\app\\provider_catalog.py:62-62\n  The Vertex card explicitly sends users to `docs/gemini_pro_credit_setup.md`, but that file is not present in this commit or repository. Since the card requires a non-obvious Agent Platform API/key restriction setup, users following the UI cannot access the promised instructions and are likely unable to configure the new provider.\n",
